MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_001: On your own today, Promised One? I see Fortuna's\nnot with you.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_002: That's too bad. Maybe this will help.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_003: Huh?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_004: It's a bird trap. The birds enter from here and this\npart closes to prevent escape.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_005: Fortuna often turns into a bird and flies off\nsomewhere.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_006: I thought you might need to snare her so you can\ntend to her. You are her servant.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_007: <NCA>"I'm not her servant."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_008: Yes, I know, it's difficult when one is devoted to an\nunruly liege. With Gladius, I often... Hm?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_009: Apologies—you do serve her, yes? You've sworn\nloyalty and take her orders as mandate?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_010: If not, my mistake. I shouldn't have assumed. It's just\nthat you're always together.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_011: <NCA>"We're equals."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_012: <NCB>"I make my own decisions."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_013: <ACA>It takes confidence to count oneself as equals with\nthe Goddess of Fate. But I see.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_014: <ACA>You act of your own accord.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_015: <ACB>So you're not simply following her orders. I see.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_016: <NCA>"Is something wrong?"
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_017: I'm just interested in your sense of independence.\nI've wanted to be a knight since I was young.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_018: My ambition was always to serve. When I was\noffered the throne of Brezarant, I refused.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_019: I didn't consider myself worthy of it. Thought I could\nbetter help my country in other ways.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_020: <NCA>"You didn't want power?"
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_021: <NCB>"That's very noble of you."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_022: <ACA>No, power never much interested me, much to my\nmother's chagrin.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_023: <ACB>Oh, I don't know. If you asked my mother, she would\nsay I was just a coward.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_024: She'd been born a lesser noble but aspired to be\nqueen dowager, on the merit of my father's blood.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_025: He was connected to the royal family, and he died\nof illness. But she still saw a chance to climb.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_026: On the strength of my combat skills, I was told I\ncould take the throne.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_027: I don't know if that was true, or if it was just words,\nbut my mother believed it...
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_028: and later cursed my name for turning it down. "My\nunfilial son," she called me—until the day she died.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_029: Sometimes I wonder if I'd had more of a spine,\nhow things might have been different between us.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_030: <NCA>"You did what you thought was right."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_031: *sigh* Yes, that's true.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_032: My first loyalty is to my country. It always will be.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_033: It is the pride of my life that I put a king like\nBertrand on the throne. Someone who gives hope.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_034: <NCA>"So, there's no reason for doubt."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_035: You're exactly right. I was just...overthinking things,\nI suppose.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_A_036: Pardon my sentimentality, Promised One. I hope you\nwon't mind keeping this between us.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_001: I'll need some incense... No, maybe I ought to\nprepare rope first?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_002: Ah!
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_003: Promised One! You've returned.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_004: I presumed you'd survive, but I thought you might\nhave gotten lost.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_005: I was putting together some lures and bindings, but...\nWell, I wasn't sure what would work.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_006: <NCA>"You don't need those anymore."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_007: No, thankfully. You've saved me a lot of trouble.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_008: You intend to continue helping the people of\nthis world, yes?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_009: Well... Will you let me join you?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_010: <NCA>"I doubt you'd take no for an answer."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_011: <NCB>"You really want to leave your homeland?"
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_012: <ACA>Hahaha! True. My loyalty is hard to shake.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_013: <ACB>I've appointed one of my best as the new\nlegion commander. Everything else is squared away.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_014: I travel light, so I can leave now if you're ready.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_015: Bertrand gave his permission as well. In fact,\nhe welcomed it with open arms.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_016: The king gave his permission as well. In fact,\nhe welcomed it with open arms.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_017: I'd intended to serve him, until I realized I could do\nsomething to benefit my country more.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_018: Have you heard the legend from Sai, of the vassal\nwho set out to find the elixir of immortality?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_019: <NCA>"You want to find this elixir?"
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_020: Oh, not particularly. The point of the story is that the\nvassal travels all over the land to find it.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_021: Brezarant's goal after this war is to bring lasting\npeace to the continent, yes?
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_022: Well, you can't bring peace to a land you don't know.\nI want see all of Dagda I can.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_023: <NCA>"We'd better get going, then."
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_024: Yes, let's. Don't worry—I'm well accustomed to\nlong journeys.
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_025: <RSDS>And to blending in with different cultures. They even\nmistook me for a local in the land of Sai!
MID_SE_Ism_Gat_S_026: Hahaha... Why do you look worried all of a sudden?